  "final_response": "I fixed it, and `tests/test_parser.py::test_dates` now passes.\n\n**Cause:** `parse_date` handed its input to `split_date` from `shared/utils.py`, which only splits on `-`. So `\"2026/12/31\"` didn't split into three parts and raised a `ValueError`.\n\n**Change:** In `app/parser.py`, `parse_date` now trims the input and replaces `/` with `-` before calling `split_date`. Both `YYYY-MM-DD` and `YYYY/MM/DD` now work.\n\nI left `shared/utils.py` alone because you asked me to change only `app/parser.py`. That file also says the helper is used by the billing, imports and reports services, so changing it could affect them too.",
